From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: a Clear recorded into a command list covers the clip in force

Paint.NET 5 draws its History and Layers lists so: on the list box's
bitmap it pushes an axis-aligned clip the size of the box, makes a
command list the target, records the box's background as a Clear, makes
the bitmap the target again and draws the list through its own effect.
The clip was pushed before the list became the target, so the list did
not record it; a Clear outside any clip adds nothing to a list's bounds
(0427: Paint.NET's brush stamps clear their lists unclipped), the
effect's input was empty and nothing was drawn -- the lists were black
boxes. A Clear recorded while a clip is in force is now recorded inside
that clip (pushed, cleared, popped), as Direct2D bounds it.

Test: test/d2dfx-gate.sh, cmdlist_clipped_clear_bounds and
cmdlist_clipped_clear_effect (mutant SG_MUTANT_D2D_LIST_CLEAR_UNCLIPPED).
---
--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -2134,6 +2134,40 @@
 
     if (context->target.type == D2D_TARGET_COMMAND_LIST)
     {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_D2D_LIST_CLEAR_UNCLIPPED
+        /* A Clear covers the clip in force, also one pushed before the
+         * list became the target: it is recorded inside that clip, so the
+         * list's bounds hold it (Paint.NET clips to a list box, records
+         * the box's background as a Clear and draws the list through an
+         * effect; unclipped, the effect had nothing to draw: black). */
+        if (context->clip_stack.count)
+        {
+            const D2D1_RECT_F *clip = &context->clip_stack.stack[context->clip_stack.count - 1];
+            float x_scale = context->desc.dpiX / 96.0f, y_scale = context->desc.dpiY / 96.0f;
+            D2D1_MATRIX_3X2_F inverse;
+            D2D1_POINT_2F point;
+            D2D1_RECT_F local;
+
+            if (d2d_matrix_invert(&inverse, &context->drawing_state.transform))
+            {
+                d2d_point_transform(&point, &inverse, clip->left, clip->top);
+                d2d_rect_set(&local, point.x / x_scale, point.y / y_scale, point.x / x_scale, point.y / y_scale);
+                d2d_point_transform(&point, &inverse, clip->left, clip->bottom);
+                point.x /= x_scale; point.y /= y_scale;
+                d2d_rect_expand(&local, &point);
+                d2d_point_transform(&point, &inverse, clip->right, clip->top);
+                point.x /= x_scale; point.y /= y_scale;
+                d2d_rect_expand(&local, &point);
+                d2d_point_transform(&point, &inverse, clip->right, clip->bottom);
+                point.x /= x_scale; point.y /= y_scale;
+                d2d_rect_expand(&local, &point);
+                d2d_command_list_push_clip(context->target.command_list, &local, D2D1_ANTIALIAS_MODE_ALIASED);
+                d2d_command_list_clear(context->target.command_list, colour);
+                d2d_command_list_pop_clip(context->target.command_list);
+                return;
+            }
+        }
+#endif
         d2d_command_list_clear(context->target.command_list, colour);
         return;
     }
